  "request_sha256": "8a2e13f228b2f1a1578ee8c803e18f264cb325b0bb7b6a7c905382a06e5a840a",
  "answer": "{\"type\":\"selection\",\"packet_sha256\":\"e66f9bc5c8d3c38c171ce5f2b71ec8db539892c59cc816c1bd1f4cbb0dc982c6\",\"batch_strategy\":\"Condition-response and failure-repair batch combining loading contrasts, strong-composition endpoint probes, local functional-group neighborhoods, and compact controls.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"3418b1a160c0848777ce\",\"reason\":\"m22 provides an ordinary aromatic ester anchor for calibrating central solvent and loading response.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4c15c048e4f33116df8d\",\"reason\":\"Low-composition m144 supplies a compact nitrile boundary control for lower-endpoint calibration.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4ee0e15840492362f7d8\",\"reason\":\"m34 at 1/1 adds a routine halogenated aromatic ketone point for separating ordinary behavior from strong-condition tails.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"dbe79bb4ca4ae4967721\",\"reason\":\"m12 at 5/1 tests compact hydrocarbon behavior at moderate composition and broadens weak-interaction calibration.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"09f7ce5c473ea7ea5d94\",\"reason\":\"m85 at 10/1 probes a strong-condition aromatic ester regime with a broad predicted endpoint interval.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"cd223aa386d14587c91c\",\"reason\":\"m154 at 5/1 tests whether a halogenated ether-like scaffold remains compact across density and loading.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"2e07c48e8a35741ba001\",\"reason\":\"m16 supplies a routine low-polarity ester response point without introducing an extreme interaction motif.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"00a82096f4ac4e03ea01\",\"reason\":\"m10 at 50/1 is a nonpolar diaryl control for testing whether strong composition alone creates delayed endpoints.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"d074d3b670ffc9e13369\",\"reason\":\"Low-composition m136 supplies a compact weakly interacting aromatic boundary control.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"fefecd79dc057980f62c\",\"reason\":\"m81 at 5/1 tests a polar aromatic ester or ketone neighborhood with a wide predicted V2 range.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"15a51cf39e266a0aeb52\",\"reason\":\"m54 at low composition provides an ordinary aromatic ketone anchor that limits global endpoint inflation.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"105457e008d11073c7b7\",\"reason\":\"High-composition m97 adds a hydrophobic aromatic ester point in a delayed predicted regime.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"605436d35600502e8c2e\",\"reason\":\"m30 at 50/1 is a strong-composition aromatic ketone control for testing scaffold-specific endpoint expansion.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"ade362756cf5f89aea03\",\"reason\":\"m203 probes a donor-containing cyclic alcohol scaffold and adds loading-sensitive central coverage.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"51691caac0be166b02c7\",\"reason\":\"m202 supplies a structurally unusual phosphorus-containing acceptor point with high condition novelty and polar-scaffold coverage.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"c096c324a71974b6ab37\",\"reason\":\"m34 at 50/1 and higher sample volume directly tests whether a weakly interacting halogenated aromatic develops a genuine delayed tail.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"476647879af7df57d509\",\"reason\":\"m75 at 2/1 extends diester response coverage and separates ordinary acceptor-rich behavior from long endpoint regimes.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"c17fee6d4419cf961d3a\",\"reason\":\"m5 at 20/1 is a compact dihalogenated aromatic control at strong composition.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"b33b7253147a64c9baeb\",\"reason\":\"m137 at 50/1 tests compact heavy-halogen behavior at strong composition.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"34e3e4807176cfd57e57\",\"reason\":\"m126 at 50/1 probes whether a simple aromatic ether remains compact in a strong mobile phase.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"a04af55e394c31f4123a\",\"reason\":\"m192 at 20/1 adds a high-composition aromatic aldehyde point in a sparse local functional-group neighborhood.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"22917c7639323bc6f051\",\"reason\":\"m8 extends brominated heteroaromatic coverage and tests transfer between oxygen-containing aromatic environments.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"117874b15293a4b5e3e1\",\"reason\":\"m128 probes sulfur-containing aromatic carbonyl behavior and separates heteroatom effects from global polarity.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"b1b6f6ec4f613144aba4\",\"reason\":\"m104 at 1/1 and higher sample volume supplies a local aniline-benzoate graph-context point between compact and delayed behavior.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"9aadc8feed825d13a5d7\",\"reason\":\"m4 at 1/1 and 150 uL adds an extended fused-aromatic control for learning whether aromatic surface area alone broadens V2.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"084212942b840ae3c1c7\",\"reason\":\"m34 at 10/1 and lower sample volume forms a condition-loading contrast and tests response curvature.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"f46da3c00b2199795e4c\",\"reason\":\"m169 at 50/1 probes a halogenated carbonyl-like scaffold in a high predicted endpoint regime.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"fe7d7af2c919facfe5f5\",\"reason\":\"m209 at 10/1 tests donor-acceptor and trifluoroether context in a sparse phenol neighborhood.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"90b458cad40e4d8b82fd\",\"reason\":\"m157 at 2/1 provides a compact heavy-halogen control to separate molecular weight from silica interaction.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"cacb6e56d0b2fc61cde2\",\"reason\":\"m22 at 10/1 extends the aromatic ester response curve and tests whether composition effects transfer smoothly across loading.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4da6e3b93f29af1efa94\",\"reason\":\"m198 at 5/1 adds a nitrobenzaldehyde-like point for local condition-response and endpoint calibration.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"cc1f4899902d6f44bef2\",\"reason\":\"m28 at low composition adds an acetoxy aldehyde neighborhood point and separates local carbonyl context from global polarity.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null}],\"hypotheses\":[],\"feedback_interpretation\":\"Recent feedback strengthened the distinction between genuine long endpoints in polar or extended families and unsupported tails in compact aromatic, nitrile, and halogenated controls. It also highlighted abrupt or loading-sensitive response curves, especially for extended aromatic and acceptor-rich families. This batch emphasizes local condition and loading contrasts while preserving compact boundary controls.\",\"batch_rationale\":\"The batch combines strong-condition extrapolation points, loading contrasts, local aldehyde and heteroaromatic neighborhoods, and compact controls. It repairs endpoint underprediction in responsive families, tests whether condition effects are smooth or threshold-like, and limits global overcorrection by sampling weakly interacting aromatic, nitrile, and halogenated scaffolds. These labels should improve Row-distribution generalization by teaching when retention depends on solvent strength, loading, or local graph context.\"}",
